{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"f3f1717d663704ab","name":"card_event_through_the_ice","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Finland/events/card_event_through_the_ice","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"THROUGH THE ICE","text":"Deal 2 damage to a unit and each other unit with the same name.","flavorText":"During the Winter War (November 1939 - March 1940), numerous lakes in Finland were covered by a thick layer of ice. This offered the Soviet invading forces extensive areas to move troops safely away from the sniper-laden forests. Finnish engineers used to embed mines beneath the ice, in order to help guard frozen rivers and lakes during winter time. These mines were detonated when enemy formations crossed the ice, often sending Soviet soldiers and equipment to a watery grave. As a result, Red Army commanders stopped moving large numbers of troops across frozen lakes. Instead they moved their troops through nearby forests where Finnish snipers and machine gunners would patiently await their targets.","faction":"Finland","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_through_the_ice","title":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_through_the_ice_title","SourceString":"THROUGH THE ICE","LocalizedString":"THROUGH THE ICE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Finland","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_through_the_ice_text","SourceString":"Deal 2 damage to a unit and each other unit with the same name.","LocalizedString":"Deal 2 damage to a unit and each other unit with the same name."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_through_the_ice_history","SourceString":"During the Winter War (November 1939 - March 1940), numerous lakes in Finland were covered by a thick layer of ice. This offered the Soviet invading forces extensive areas to move troops safely away from the sniper-laden forests. Finnish engineers used to embed mines beneath the ice, in order to help guard frozen rivers and lakes during winter time. These mines were detonated when enemy formations crossed the ice, often sending Soviet soldiers and equipment to a watery grave. As a result, Red Army commanders stopped moving large numbers of troops across frozen lakes. Instead they moved their troops through nearby forests where Finnish snipers and machine gunners would patiently await their targets.","LocalizedString":"During the Winter War (November 1939 - March 1940), numerous lakes in Finland were covered by a thick layer of ice. This offered the Soviet invading forces extensive areas to move troops safely away from the sniper-laden forests. Finnish engineers used to embed mines beneath the ice, in order to help guard frozen rivers and lakes during winter time. These mines were detonated when enemy formations crossed the ice, often sending Soviet soldiers and equipment to a watery grave. As a result, Red Army commanders stopped moving large numbers of troops across frozen lakes. Instead they moved their troops through nearby forests where Finnish snipers and machine gunners would patiently await their targets."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_5_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Cues/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_5_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Finland/t_ice.t_ice","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Look and Learn","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/THROUGH_THE_ICE.THROUGH_THE_ICE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":330.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_through_the_ice_photo","SourceString":"A Finnish soldier with a reindeer, crossing a frozen lake in northern Lapland, Fi